# STATE.md and WORK.md are GENERATED by scripts/board.py and carry a checksum of their
# own body. Every branch that opens, finishes or edits a work item changes them, so every
# pair of concurrent branches conflicts on them -- reliably, and for no information: the
# correct result is never a blend of the two sides, it is whatever board.py produces from
# the merged inputs.
#
# Resolving that by hand also silently breaks the checksum, which then makes
# `board.py --check` refuse to overwrite ("edited by hand") in whichever session next
# runs it -- a failure two steps removed from its cause.
#
# So: do not merge them. Regenerate them. These drivers run scripts/board.py and take its
# output, whatever either side said. One driver per file because `%P` (the path being
# merged) needs git >= 2.44 and this repo has run on 2.43.
#
# The drivers are registered by `python3 scripts/board.py setup` (see CLAUDE.md). Without
# it git falls back to an ordinary text merge, which conflicts -- noisily, not silently,
# which is the right way round.
STATE.md merge=board-state
WORK.md  merge=board-work

# Detector outputs and goldens are large single-line-ish JSON. A textual merge of two
# sides of one of these is never correct and is not always a conflict (Lesson 32: a
# clean merge is not evidence). Refuse to auto-merge; make a human choose.
results/canonical/*.json   -merge
results/rulers/*.json      -merge
results/expert_lists/*.json -merge
docs/golden/v7/baseline_ketubot.json -merge
